      "raw": "After analyzing all views and their corresponding mask regions, we observe that each mask region (R001 through R007) corresponds to a portion of the same garment \u2014 a long, form-fitting, pink, beaded or sequined slip dress with thin spaghetti straps and a low back. The dress is shown from multiple angles: front, back, side, and close-up, and in one view as a flat lay. The fabric is consistently a sheer, textured pink material with a dense, sparkling embellishment pattern. The silhouette is consistent: a full-length, body-hugging dress with a scoop neckline and open back.\n\nAll mask regions (R001 to R007) show parts of this same garment, even if cropped or from different perspectives. There is no evidence of a second garment \u2014 no undershirt, no separate layer, no different fabric or construction. The regions are all from the same dress, just captured in different views and crops.\n\nTherefore, we can confidently assign all regions to a single garment track.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tracks\": [\n    {\n      \"garment\": \"A long, form-fitting, pink, beaded or sequined slip dress with thin spaghetti straps and a low back, made of a sheer, textured fabric with a dense sparkling embellishment pattern.\",\n      \"regions\": [\n        \"R001\",\n        \"R002\",\n        \"R003\",\n        \"R004\",\n        \"R005\",\n        \"R006\",\n        \"R007\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
